<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-L59) maps every equation — DITH Eq. 1, the Krieg regimes, Young-Dupré Eq. 1 and the four Pass 3 Nodal relations — to its source and names the Lean theorem backing the closure; each Nodal function docstring (L232-L334) states its formula, its sources and the Lean declaration it mirrors; `simulate_nodal_coupled_internalization` (L776-L800) states the reduction assumptions (tier-of-origin memory, margin at the bottom, MCS -> hpf linear); the self-test comments (L1760-L1800) name the Lean theorem each check corresponds to, and the math KG yaml registers 6 equations with `code_locus` / `lean_locus`. Deductions: the lattice-energy scale `g_scale = 5.0`, `j_hom = 4.0`, the swap temperature factor 2.2 and the 3-layer bias 0.35 / temperature 12.0 remain uncited numerics (L496-L497, L557, L713-L714) (-5); the classification thresholds (72.5 / 112.5 pN/um, L336-L343) are midpoints by construction, not sourced (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py L496–L497: g_scale and j_hom lattice scale constants without a citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py#L496-L497>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Brodland (2002) Eq. (1) is implemented exactly in `compute_dith_tensions` (L136-L184) and now also in continuous per-cell form in the Nodal-coupled sorter: `_cell_pair_J` (L840-L847) rebuilds the bond matrix every MCS from gamma_i0 = beta_i and gamma_ij = kappa|beta_i - beta_j|, which is Brodland's law with omega_ij = beta_i + beta_j - gamma_ij, and Lean theorem 5 proves the closure always satisfies the Krieg regime-I inequality 0 < gamma_ij < |gamma_i0 - gamma_j0|. The Nodal coupling (L232-L334) is a recognisable reduced morphogen model: exponential range, first-order temporal rise from sphere stage, two-threshold Hill dose response mirroring Krieg's own lefty1 / cyclops / cyclops+casanova induction, first-order cortex relaxation; Lean theorems 4 and 6 prove monotonicity/bounds of the dose map and non-overshoot of the relaxation step. Deductions: the static regimes (L496-L508) use j_hom = 4.0 for both E-E and M-M contacts, discarding the gamma_EE = 70 / gamma_MM = 150 that `compute_dith_tensions` returns, so the static lattice energy is a Steinberg-type J matrix and not Brodland's full DITH energy (-4); the Nodal field is 1D and exposure is frozen to the tier of origin (L826, L893), with no Lefty feedback or epiboly (-3); kappa = 2/3 is a phenomenological closure tuned to gamma_EM = 30 (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py L496–L508: Static regimes: j_hom = 4.0 shared by E-E and M-M bonds; gamma_EE / gamma_MM from compute_dith_tensions are not used in the energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py#L496-L508>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1595-L1702) returns 13 measurements with non-null references: the 8 v2 ones (gamma_EM = 30, beta_M - beta_E = 45, wild-type Delta_r = +0.3807 vs 0.34, caMLCK Delta_r = -0.3282 vs -0.34, Blebbistatin 0, 3-layer gap 0.4237 vs 0.42, Young-Dupré 0.866, profile r = 0.9301 vs 0.92) and 5 new Nodal ones: shield mesendoderm tiers 5 (ref 5), shield endoderm tiers 2 (ref 2), hierarchy established 4.87 hpf (ref <= 6.0), Nodal-coupled Delta_r = +0.3504 (ref 0.34), Nodal-null |Delta_r| = 0 (ref 0). The hard-coded \"p=0.0001\" strings of v2 are gone (L1625 now states single-seed / no replicate statistics; L1660 reports the computed Pearson p). Deductions: the two tier-count references and the 0.34 / 0.42 radial anchors are recalled approximate literature values, not digitised from a figure or table, and the hierarchy reference is only an upper bound (-7); all sorting metrics come from one seed with no replicate spread (-3); the Nodal tier counts are partly tautological because lambda and K_M were chosen to hit them (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py L1666–L1680: Tier-count references (5, 2) are recalled approximate values; method strings say so <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py#L1666-L1680>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-blebbistatin-control-radial-separation>,
